  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 0.88,
      "end": 13.88,
      "text": "This very evening, archive sessions from 1970 and 1971 by the original lineup of Mott the Hoofle, and a repeat of one of our recent sets by the band who are going to support Judas Priest on their Spring UK tour, the band called Iron Maiden.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.88,
      "end": 37.55,
      "text": "We've got classic cuts by Yes, The Only Ones, ELP, and RDO Speedwagon, and new releases by Utopia, John Fox, Aerosmith, Rush, Girl, Jon and Vangelis, and the Tigers of Pantang.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.55,
      "end": 39.33,
      "text": "not forgetting our Friday Night Connection,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.39,
      "end": 42.31,
      "text": "the answer to last week's and a new one for this week.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 42.61,
      "end": 45.09,
      "text": "But this week, we start with a new single by Queen.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 50.7,
      "end": 57.3,
      "text": "And that's the new single by Triumph that's just come out,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 57.3,
      "end": 175.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 57.3,
      "end": 175.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 180.0,
      "end": 355.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 180.0,
      "end": 355.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 360.0,
      "end": 454.35,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 360.0,
      "end": 454.35,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 454.35,
      "end": 457.33,
      "text": "the Canadian band that is called American Girls.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 457.75,
      "end": 461.21,
      "text": "It's off their album that came out in 1979, entitled Just Again.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 463.05,
      "end": 464.79,
      "text": "And it was especially for Vivian.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 465.39,
      "end": 469.69,
      "text": "And also for a gentleman by the name of Peter Russell",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 469.69,
      "end": 471.71,
      "text": "and his future wife, Beverly Sheaf.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 471.71,
      "end": 475.33,
      "text": "It seems they're getting married tomorrow at 12.05 p.m.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 475.65,
      "end": 477.43,
      "text": "And I've got to wish them all the best for the future",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 477.43,
      "end": 480.87,
      "text": "and loads of happiness from a gentleman by the name of Philip Russell.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 481.67,
      "end": 483.71,
      "text": "And on the air, I must mention Red Eye.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 486.49,
      "end": 489.45,
      "text": "And it seems that that's some sort of clue to the household,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 489.57,
      "end": 492.65,
      "text": "the [redacted address], Waterloo in Leeds 12.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 495.89,
      "end": 499.39,
      "text": "This came out in 1969, and when I first played it this afternoon,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 499.51,
      "end": 501.37,
      "text": "I hadn't, I think, heard it since then.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 501.45,
      "end": 503.43,
      "text": "And it's delightful. It's yes.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 503.43,
      "end": 506.43,
      "text": "And that's John and Vangelis",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 540.0,
      "end": 895.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 540.0,
      "end": 895.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 900.0,
      "end": 1024.29,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 900.0,
      "end": 1024.29,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1024.29,
      "end": 1026.65,
      "text": "And a short track from the album Short Stories",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1026.65,
      "end": 1028.17,
      "text": "Which is out at the moment on Polydor",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1028.17,
      "end": 1030.87,
      "text": "The track is called Far Away in Baguade",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1030.87,
      "end": 1033.44,
      "text": "And before that something from 1969",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1033.44,
      "end": 1035.48,
      "text": "From the first album ever put out by Yes",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1035.48,
      "end": 1037.56,
      "text": "It was the track known as Survival",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1037.56,
      "end": 1040.72,
      "text": "I played it specially for a lady who was all of five years of age when it came out",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1040.72,
      "end": 1043.24,
      "text": "And I say a lady because she writes a beautiful letter",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1043.24,
      "end": 1044.04,
      "text": "Her name is Sue",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1044.04,
      "end": 1047.3,
      "text": "And she lives at [redacted address]. Furgrove, Wollaston",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1047.3,
      "end": 1049.18,
      "text": "Starbridge in the West Midlands",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1049.18,
      "end": 1052.32,
      "text": "And she writes at the back of her letter here",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1052.32,
      "end": 1056.4,
      "text": "all about critics and she goes on to knock all the critics because all the critics knock yes",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1056.4,
      "end": 1061.6,
      "text": "but then she reminds us that tomata was put down by one man writing in sounds but he wasn't right",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1061.6,
      "end": 1066.26,
      "text": "he got to number three in the melody maker poll honestly sue i think critics half the time don't",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1066.26,
      "end": 1069.7,
      "text": "know what they're talking about including me when i get on something like round table",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1069.7,
      "end": 1071.94,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1069.7,
      "end": 1071.94,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1076.94,
      "end": 1088.94,
      "text": "it's 10 18 and here's iron maiden good band they were the only ones that came out in 1978 from",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1088.94,
      "end": 1435.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1088.94,
      "end": 1435.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1440.0,
      "end": 1534.88,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1440.0,
      "end": 1534.88,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1535.14,
      "end": 1537.56,
      "text": "Right, let's get down to our archives session now.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1537.68,
      "end": 1539.56,
      "text": "Recorded during 1970 and 1971,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1539.88,
      "end": 1543.22,
      "text": "here's the original line-up of Mott the Hoople and Three Cuts.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1543.48,
      "end": 1546.52,
      "text": "And here's a new progressive crew that makes a welcome addition to the scene,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1546.94,
      "end": 1547.56,
      "text": "Mott the Hoople.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1551.35,
      "end": 1553.79,
      "text": "This is a number written by groups organist Mick Ralph,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1553.85,
      "end": 1555.77,
      "text": "and it's called Thunder Buck Ram.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1557.53,
      "end": 1563.53,
      "text": "...Watts, Dale Griffin, Mick Ralphs, Verdon Allen, and Ian Un...",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1563.53,
      "end": 2117.84,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1563.53,
      "end": 2117.84,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2117.84,
      "end": 2121.1,
      "text": "Ah, as we've always called him, Mott the Hoople, recorded in 70 and 71.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2121.1,
      "end": 2122.5,
      "text": "three cuts by them",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2122.5,
      "end": 2126.12,
      "text": "the original Mixed Up Kid, Whiskey Woman and Thunderbuck Ram",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2126.12,
      "end": 2127.56,
      "text": "more from Mott the Hoople later",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2127.56,
      "end": 2129.8,
      "text": "you know, we don't spend the rest of the week",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2129.8,
      "end": 2133.06,
      "text": "sitting around on the wonderful sunny shores of the Serpentine",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2133.06,
      "end": 2135.4,
      "text": "you know, sort of lazing it",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2135.4,
      "end": 2137.92,
      "text": "we actually do scurry around the record companies",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2137.92,
      "end": 2138.9,
      "text": "looking for new product",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2138.9,
      "end": 2140.96,
      "text": "and this week we've found some",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2140.96,
      "end": 2142.68,
      "text": "that you're going to like, I know",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2142.68,
      "end": 2143.92,
      "text": "it's Utopia",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2143.92,
      "end": 2146.92,
      "text": "phenomenally talented bunch of people",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2520.0,
      "end": 2825.95,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2520.0,
      "end": 2825.95,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2825.95,
      "end": 2827.01,
      "text": "that's Utopia",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2827.01,
      "end": 2831.02,
      "text": "And a track from an album that's coming out on February the 15th",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2831.02,
      "end": 2832.82,
      "text": "The album's called Adventures in Utopia",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2832.82,
      "end": 2836.06,
      "text": "And the cuts that you heard were Last of the New Wave Riders",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2836.06,
      "end": 2837.86,
      "text": "And Caravan",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2837.86,
      "end": 2840.94,
      "text": "And that made a gentleman by the name of Matthew Jeffries",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2840.94,
      "end": 2842.78,
      "text": "Of [redacted address] in Bath",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2842.78,
      "end": 2844.78,
      "text": "Deliriously happy I would think this evening",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2844.78,
      "end": 2847.02,
      "text": "Because he's been waiting for that album for ages",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2847.02,
      "end": 2850.42,
      "text": "So let me tell you, it comes out once again on February the 15th",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2850.98,
      "end": 2852.5,
      "text": "Adventures in Utopia",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2852.5,
      "end": 2854.84,
      "text": "By Utopia, led of course by Todd Rundgren",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2854.84,
      "end": 2860.34,
      "text": "13 minutes before 11 o'clock",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2860.34,
      "end": 2867.28,
      "text": "now the next track coming up is by elp and it's specially for dill g non and mez and hickey and",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2867.28,
      "end": 2873.5,
      "text": "barb and pete and everybody at the manse group from dill of number nine hussy road brown hills",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2873.5,
      "end": 2878.76,
      "text": "in walsall who wants to say hello to all the other dills listening it's also for steve atkinson of",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2878.76,
      "end": 2890.76,
      "text": "sheffield and for robert hunter who lives in chin or in oxen and it's called i guess you could call",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2890.76,
      "end": 3415.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2890.76,
      "end": 3415.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3420.0,
      "end": 3552.09,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3420.0,
      "end": 3552.09,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3552.09,
      "end": 3556.11,
      "text": "it that's john fox who'll be on rock on saturday tomorrow having a chat a track from his latest",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3556.11,
      "end": 3560.91,
      "text": "album is called metamatic and the track you heard was no one driving and before that something from",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3560.91,
      "end": 3567.33,
      "text": "1973 a real sort of old wave classic to listen to from brain salad surgery elp emerson lake and",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3567.33,
      "end": 3577.53,
      "text": "palmer and toccato but now iron maiden three little track from a brand new album by aerosmith",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3780.0,
      "end": 3991.73,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3780.0,
      "end": 3991.73,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3991.73,
      "end": 3995.61,
      "text": "the album is called night in the ruts which is a good name for a band and the track was entitled",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3995.61,
      "end": 3999.67,
      "text": "no surprise and i love the little bit that's written down here that says it's a vindaloo",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3999.67,
      "end": 4005.76,
      "text": "production before that iron maiden and running free something you might like to know just after",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4005.76,
      "end": 4010.14,
      "text": "six o'clock tomorrow we've got a live link up with a gentleman who lives at the moment over",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4010.14,
      "end": 4015.02,
      "text": "there in hollywood his name is roger waters of the pink floyd now that's going to happen just",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4015.02,
      "end": 4019.8,
      "text": "after six o'clock tomorrow on rock on saturday and one of the questions i'm going to be asking",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4019.8,
      "end": 4027.76,
      "text": "him is about what gigs and indeed where will the gigs be this year for the floyd so don't miss",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4027.76,
      "end": 4032.32,
      "text": "that just about three minutes past six i think it's set up for tomorrow on rock on saturday",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4032.32,
      "end": 4038.97,
      "text": "chat with mr roger waters right start of the friday night connection tracks we played last",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4038.97,
      "end": 4044.65,
      "text": "week were racing in a by steve hackett from the lp please don't touch illusions in g major by",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4044.65,
      "end": 4051.7,
      "text": "elo from el dorado and the other track was in soda f by brand x from the lp product answer",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4051.7,
      "end": 4052.6,
      "text": "simple",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4052.6,
      "end": 4053.6,
      "text": "A",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4053.6,
      "end": 4055.82,
      "text": "well they're all keys aren't they",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4055.82,
      "end": 4056.44,
      "text": "A",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4056.44,
      "end": 4057.58,
      "text": "G",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4057.58,
      "end": 4058.32,
      "text": "and F",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4058.32,
      "end": 4059.54,
      "text": "and if you like E as well",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4059.54,
      "end": 4060.56,
      "text": "the E from E-L-O",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4060.56,
      "end": 4063.32,
      "text": "keys or musical notes",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4063.32,
      "end": 4064.62,
      "text": "and the gentleman who got it right",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4064.62,
      "end": 4067.4,
      "text": "and sent in a very very well illustrated card",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4067.4,
      "end": 4068.64,
      "text": "is Les Scott",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4068.64,
      "end": 4070.78,
      "text": "of 41A Dublin Street Edinburgh in Scotland",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4070.78,
      "end": 4072.5,
      "text": "Les you got yourself a ten pound record token",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4072.5,
      "end": 4079.42,
      "text": "and also Mr Scott",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4079.42,
      "end": 4080.92,
      "text": "up there in Scotland",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4080.92,
      "end": 4082.7,
      "text": "has put together a Friday night connection",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4082.7,
      "end": 4084.34,
      "text": "three bits of music",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4084.34,
      "end": 4086.47,
      "text": "with a theme and or connection",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4086.47,
      "end": 4089.87,
      "text": "And this week, just to be kind to you, it's pretty simple.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4089.87,
      "end": 4990.31,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4089.87,
      "end": 4990.31,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4990.31,
      "end": 4992.39,
      "text": "But unfortunately, it's the wrong one.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4993.35,
      "end": 4997.29,
      "text": "I should really there have played Space Station No. 5 by Montrose,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4997.39,
      "end": 5001.29,
      "text": "but like the silly little twit I turned out to be, I played Bad Motor Scooter.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5001.55,
      "end": 5006.19,
      "text": "So if you can just imagine that the last four or five minutes were filled with Space Station No. 5",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5006.19,
      "end": 5007.43,
      "text": "instead of Bad Motor Scooter,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5007.43,
      "end": 5011.27,
      "text": "then you'll have some idea as to exactly what the Friday Night Connection is all about.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5012.6,
      "end": 5014.42,
      "text": "So here I sit, blushing,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5015.2,
      "end": 5016.3,
      "text": "feeling like a fool,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5016.82,
      "end": 5019.68,
      "text": "and thinking that the expression on Les Scott's face up there",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5019.68,
      "end": 5021.86,
      "text": "of 41A Dublin Street in Edinburgh, Scotland",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5021.86,
      "end": 5024.76,
      "text": "must be one of absolute, total consternation.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5025.84,
      "end": 5026.96,
      "text": "But let me just go back on that.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5027.08,
      "end": 5028.06,
      "text": "Played the wrong track there.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5028.2,
      "end": 5029.94,
      "text": "That should have been Space Station No. 5.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5031.0,
      "end": 5033.38,
      "text": "Nonetheless, the other two were right for a change.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5033.92,
      "end": 5035.61,
      "text": "And if you could figure it all out,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5035.63,
      "end": 5038.11,
      "text": "you'll find your Friday night connection in those three bits of music.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5038.61,
      "end": 5038.93,
      "text": "Whack them.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5039.65,
      "end": 5041.81,
      "text": "Whack it all down on a postcard and send it to",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5041.81,
      "end": 5043.79,
      "text": "Thomas the Idiot Vance",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5043.79,
      "end": 5045.55,
      "text": "The Friday Night Connection",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5045.55,
      "end": 5046.71,
      "text": "The Friday Rock Show",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5046.71,
      "end": 5048.03,
      "text": "BBC Radio 1",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5048.03,
      "end": 5050.53,
      "text": "London W1A4WW",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5050.53,
      "end": 5053.11,
      "text": "And if we pick your card or letter out of the bag",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5053.11,
      "end": 5054.67,
      "text": "you get yourself a £10 record token",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5054.67,
      "end": 5056.73,
      "text": "and a chance to kick me in parts",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5056.73,
      "end": 5058.65,
      "text": "where I probably will feel a bit tender",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5058.65,
      "end": 5061.36,
      "text": "And don't forget to put together your own",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5061.36,
      "end": 5062.88,
      "text": "Friday Night Connection as well, please",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5062.88,
      "end": 5064.81,
      "text": "Sorry about that",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5064.81,
      "end": 5067.43,
      "text": "Radio 1 Stereo",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5067.43,
      "end": 5069.73,
      "text": "They'll soon be sending me to Transylvania",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5069.73,
      "end": 5073.93,
      "text": "Good little single that's kicking you around",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5462.11,
      "end": 5464.95,
      "text": "on the Neat Record label, Neat Records, that is.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5465.33,
      "end": 5467.09,
      "text": "It's by the Tigers of Pantang,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5467.27,
      "end": 5469.27,
      "text": "and its title is Don't Touch Me There.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5469.73,
      "end": 5472.87,
      "text": "OK, back to the 25th of the 10th of 1971",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5472.87,
      "end": 5475.41,
      "text": "for two more from Mott the Hoople.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5475.41,
      "end": 5953.89,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5475.41,
      "end": 5953.89,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5953.89,
      "end": 5956.05,
      "text": "Recording back in 1971, Mott the Hoople",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5956.05,
      "end": 5958.33,
      "text": "and Moon Upstairs and Darkness, Darkness,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5958.53,
      "end": 5959.71,
      "text": "our archive sessions tonight,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5959.81,
      "end": 5961.61,
      "text": "especially for Timothy Walls, I think it is, of Kent,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5962.01,
      "end": 5965.69,
      "text": "and also for Colin Servant, who lives up there in Liverpool.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5965.95,
      "end": 5968.23,
      "text": "Next week, our archive sets by Roy Harper.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5968.81,
      "end": 5979.01,
      "text": "And if you listen to the show next week, you can hear their first ever radio session.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6120.0,
      "end": 6295.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6120.0,
      "end": 6295.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6300.0,
      "end": 6608.97,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6300.0,
      "end": 6608.97,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6608.97,
      "end": 6611.21,
      "text": "That's Girl, who are going to be on tour with UFO.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6611.91,
      "end": 6613.91,
      "text": "And a track from their album that's just come out on Jet.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6614.25,
      "end": 6617.59,
      "text": "The album is called Sheer Greed, and the track was Little Miss Anne.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6618.05,
      "end": 6620.97,
      "text": "Before that, a track from an album that's, well, I think it's been out a week now.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6621.35,
      "end": 6624.23,
      "text": "Permanent Waves, Rush for the Band, and the track was Entre Nous.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6624.65,
      "end": 6626.93,
      "text": "And prior to that, a single that's just come on the market today.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6626.93,
      "end": 6630.53,
      "text": "The single by ACDC called Touch Too Much.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6630.67,
      "end": 6632.95,
      "text": "Quick reminder that if you'd like a request played on the program,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6632.95,
      "end": 6635.13,
      "text": "simplicity personified. All we need",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6635.13,
      "end": 6637.11,
      "text": "is the, well, the name of the item that you want",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6637.11,
      "end": 6639.09,
      "text": "played. Send it to Tommy Vance,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6639.21,
      "end": 6640.75,
      "text": "the Friday Rock Show, BBC,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6641.15,
      "end": 6643.31,
      "text": "Radio 1, London, W1A",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6643.31,
      "end": 6645.11,
      "text": "4WW, and we'll do",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6645.11,
      "end": 6645.53,
      "text": "the rest.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6646.63,
      "end": 6651.43,
      "text": "A speed wagon from mine lives, and back",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7020.0,
      "end": 7193.02,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 7020.0,
      "end": 7193.02,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 7193.02,
      "end": 7194.72,
      "text": "on the road again, especially for Stephen Connor,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7194.92,
      "end": 7197.04,
      "text": "and Neil Davidson, and Ian McKenzie,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7197.52,
      "end": 7199.02,
      "text": "and all the other heavy metal freaks",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7199.02,
      "end": 7200.5,
      "text": "of Beardsden Academy in Glasgow.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7201.75,
      "end": 7203.23,
      "text": "Hope you enjoyed our sessions tonight,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7203.39,
      "end": 7205.27,
      "text": "Iron Maiden and Mod the Hoople. Don't forget",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7205.27,
      "end": 7205.85,
      "text": "that Iron Maiden",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7205.85,
      "end": 7206.57,
      "text": "are going on tour",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7206.57,
      "end": 7207.49,
      "text": "with Praying Mantis",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7207.49,
      "end": 7209.27,
      "text": "starting February the 1st",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7209.27,
      "end": 7210.19,
      "text": "at Aberdeen University.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7210.93,
      "end": 7212.31,
      "text": "And then they'll be on tour",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7212.31,
      "end": 7213.07,
      "text": "later this year",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7213.07,
      "end": 7213.81,
      "text": "with Judas Priest.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7215.47,
      "end": 7216.15,
      "text": "Next week,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7216.19,
      "end": 7216.99,
      "text": "we've got the first ever",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7216.99,
      "end": 7217.75,
      "text": "session by Girl",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7217.75,
      "end": 7219.01,
      "text": "and archive sessions",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7219.01,
      "end": 7219.95,
      "text": "from Roy Harper.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7220.79,
      "end": 7221.41,
      "text": "On Monday,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7221.51,
      "end": 7222.03,
      "text": "the Peelers got",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7222.03,
      "end": 7222.71,
      "text": "Leighton Buzzards",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7222.71,
      "end": 7223.43,
      "text": "and Lena Lovitch.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7223.57,
      "end": 7224.35,
      "text": "Don't forget Mike Reed",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7224.35,
      "end": 7225.21,
      "text": "throughout the week as well,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7225.29,
      "end": 7226.25,
      "text": "holding the flag up high.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7227.77,
      "end": 7228.67,
      "text": "Our engineer tonight",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7228.67,
      "end": 7229.15,
      "text": "was Richard.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7229.39,
      "end": 7229.87,
      "text": "Thank you, Richard.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7231.6,
      "end": 7232.4,
      "text": "Well, what more",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7232.4,
      "end": 7232.96,
      "text": "can a fellow say?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7233.04,
      "end": 7233.68,
      "text": "But tomorrow,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7233.94,
      "end": 7234.86,
      "text": "just after six o'clock,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7234.9,
      "end": 7235.8,
      "text": "I'll be chatting live",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7235.8,
      "end": 7236.92,
      "text": "to Roger Waters in Hollywood",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7236.92,
      "end": 7240.88,
      "text": "all about the dates that the Floyd are going to be doing over here during 1980.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7241.02,
      "end": 7243.06,
      "text": "Also, we'll be talking to John Fox, the Buggles and the Ramones.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7243.46,
      "end": 7244.92,
      "text": "Rock on Saturday, 4 to 7.30.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7245.32,
      "end": 7247.1,
      "text": "And now, Tony Wilson, who produces this programme,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7247.26,
      "end": 7249.88,
      "text": "will not read another filthy limerick, will you, Tony?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7250.04,
      "end": 7252.96,
      "text": "Well, after tonight, there could be a vacancy for a disc jockey.",
      "source": "Tony Wilson"
    },
    {
      "start": 7253.08,
      "end": 7255.44,
      "text": "Well, you've got a vacant one enough now.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7255.56,
      "end": 7256.34,
      "text": "I mean, what more do you want?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7256.78,
      "end": 7258.62,
      "text": "Take care, everybody. I'll see you at 4 o'clock tomorrow.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7258.72,
      "end": 7261.52,
      "text": "Until then, from Tommy Vance in London, God bless and good night.",
      "source": "TV"
    }
  ]
}